Cell[TextData[{
 "For flow visualization, the surface pressure coefficient is plotted for \
potential flow over a selected airfoil in a data file. The airfoils in this \
collection represent a small sample of the over 1500 airfoil data files \
posted on the UIUC (University of Illinois at Urbana\[Dash]Champaign) ",
 ButtonBox["Airfoil Data Site",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["http://www.ae.illinois.edu/m-selig/ads.html"], None},
  ButtonNote->"http://www.ae.illinois.edu/m-selig/ads.html"],
 ". You can vary the angle of attack (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Alpha]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineMath"],
 ") of the uniform onset flow with the airfoil. A panel method using \
straightline vortex panels of linearly varying strength and external Neumann \
boundary conditions provide the potential-flow solution. "
}], "ManipulateCaption"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The default graphic is a plot of the surface pressure coefficient. The plot \
includes values for the lift coefficient (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["C", "\[ScriptL]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineMath"],
 "), pitching moment coefficient about the leading edge (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["C", "m"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineMath"],
 "), and location of the center of pressure (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "cp"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineMath"],
 "). The yellow dot on the graph shows the location of the center of \
pressure. "
}], "ManipulateCaption",
 CellID->101511169],

Cell["\<\
Alternatively, you can chose to display a flow visualization graphic showing \
a stream plot of the velocity field. This is an important check on the \
plausibility of the potential-flow solution.\
\>", "ManipulateCaption",
 CellID->996201665],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This Demonstration is a companion to the Demonstration \"",
 ButtonBox["Potential Flow over a NACA Four Digit Airfoil",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["http://demonstrations.wolfram.com/\
PotentialFlowOverANACAFourDigitAirfoil/"], None},
  ButtonNote->
   "http://demonstrations.wolfram.com/PotentialFlowOverANACAFourDigitAirfoil/\
"],
 "\", where the airfoil geometry is specified by algebraic equations."
}], "ManipulateCaption",
 CellID->341176109],

Cell["THINGS TO TRY", "ManipulateCaption",
 CellFrame->{{0, 0}, {1, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.87, 0.87, 0.87],
 FontFamily->"Helvetica",
 FontSize->12,
 FontWeight->"Bold",
 FontColor->RGBColor[0.597406, 0, 0.0527047],
 CellTags->"ControlSuggestions"],

